title: $:/plugins/samsmith/codemirror6/readme

! CodeMirror 6 editor

Replaces TiddlyWiki's default plain-textarea tiddler editor with [[CodeMirror 6|https://codemirror.net/]], across every tiddler type: wikitext, JavaScript, CSS, HTML, JSON, Markdown, and plain text.

!! Features

* Syntax highlighting, matched to each tiddler's content type (with a purpose-built highlighter for TiddlyWiki wikitext: headings, `''bold''`, `//italic//`, `[[links]]`, `{{transclusions}}`, `<<macros>>`, code blocks, and more)
* Line numbers, active-line highlighting, and an optional code-folding gutter
* Bracket matching and auto-closing brackets/quotes
* Auto-indent, with configurable tab size and tabs-vs-spaces
* Autocomplete: typing `[[` or `{{` suggests tiddler titles, typing `<<` suggests macro/widget names, and JS/CSS/HTML get their own language-aware completions
* Find and replace (`Mod-F` to open the search panel)
* Optional Vim or Emacs keybindings, switchable from the control panel
* Editor chrome matches your active TiddlyWiki palette

Configure all of the above from ''Control panel → Settings → CodeMirror 6''.

!! Keyboard shortcuts

Besides TiddlyWiki's own tiddler-editing shortcuts (save/cancel etc.), the editor itself understands the usual CodeMirror bindings:

|!Shortcut |!Action |
|`Mod-Z` / `Mod-Shift-Z` |Undo / redo |
|`Mod-F` |Open find (and replace) |
|`Mod-G` / `Shift-Mod-G` |Find next / previous |
|`Mod-/` |Toggle line comment |
|`Mod-[` / `Mod-]` |Indent less / more |
|`Mod-Alt-\[` |Fold code at cursor (when the fold gutter is enabled) |
|`Tab` |Accept the current autocomplete suggestion, or indent |

With ''Vim'' or ''Emacs'' keybindings selected in settings, the respective editor's own key bindings take over inside the text area.

!! How it's built

This plugin bundles [[CodeMirror 6|https://codemirror.net/]] (state, view, language, autocomplete, search, and language packages for JavaScript/CSS/HTML/JSON/Markdown, plus `@replit/codemirror-vim`) into a single library tiddler with `esbuild`, and wires it up through TiddlyWiki's standard editor-engine mechanism (`$:/config/EditorTypeMappings/`, an `edit-codemirror6` widget built with `editTextWidgetFactory`, matching how the official `$:/plugins/tiddlywiki/codemirror` plugin integrates CodeMirror 5). The build sources live alongside the plugin folder in `../build`, should you want to change languages, add a highlight tag, or update dependencies and re-bundle.

!! Known limitations

* Settings changes apply to editors opened *after* the change, not to an editor already on screen.
* The wikitext highlighter is a lightweight approximation of TiddlyWiki's grammar, tuned for readability rather than 100% grammatical accuracy.
